{"authored" [{"question" "q-160866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $W$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=1.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q(x)\\in W,$ where $q(x)={x}^{2}+1.$\n- For any $p(x)\\in W$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot p(x)\\in W.$\n- The set $W$ is closed under scalar multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q(x)={x}^{2}+1\\in W$ because\n\n$$\nq(0)=(0)^{2}+1=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. There exists a function in $W$ that has a scalar multiple not in $W.$ For example, let $p(x)={x}^{2}+1$ and $k=2.$ Notice that $p(x)$ belongs to $W$ since $p(0)=1.$ However, \n\n$$\n2\\cdot p(0)=2\\cdot ({0}^{2}+1)=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n Hence, $k\\cdot p(x)\\notin W.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f8b3cb19393ca2d1dae18471d1d2d6670899615a815a11682196d00030265b43" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $h(x)\\in U,$ where $h(x)=3x.$\n- For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot p(x)\\in U.$\n- The set is closed under scalar multiplication." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $U$ contains only polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3},$ where $a$ is a real coefficient. However, $h(x)=3x$ is *not* a polynomial of this form. So, $h(x)\\notin U.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $p(x)=a{x}^{3}\\in U,$ where $a$ is a real coefficient, and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\nk\\cdot p(x)=k(a{x}^{3})=(ka){x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $(ka)$ is a real coefficient, we conclude that $(ka){x}^{3}\\in U,$ i.e., $k\\cdot p(x)\\in U.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set is closed scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f8b3cb19393ca2d1dae18471d1d2d6670899615a815a11682196d00030265b43" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-94694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $K$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=-1.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $p(x)\\in K,$ where $p(x)=(x-1)^{3}.$\n- For any $f(x),g(x)\\in K$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in K.$\n- The set is closed under addition." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $p(x)=(x-1)^{3}\\in K$ because \n\n$$\np(0)=(0-1)^{3}=(-1)^{3}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. There exist functions in $K$ such that their sum is *not* in $K.$ For example, let $f(x)=-1$ and $g(x)=(x-1)^{3}.$ Notice that both these functions belong to $K$ since $f(0)=g(0)=-1.$ However,\n\n$$\nf(0)+g(0)=-1+(0-1)^{3}=-2\\ne -1.\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x)+g(x)\\notin K.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f8b3cb19393ca2d1dae18471d1d2d6670899615a815a11682196d00030265b43" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/state.json" "file_sha256" "43e2663861d33981edf6ff452aaf3cd99ffad028ec55be9955a66cff6946df68" "basis" 1647 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-160861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/hom